#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:3
msgid "Promisify an event by waiting for it to be emitted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:5
msgid ""
"Useful when you need only one event emission and want to use it with "
"promises or await it in an async function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:7
msgid ""
"It's works with any event API in Node.js and the browser (using a "
"bundler)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:9
msgid ""
"If you want multiple individual events as they are emitted, you can use "
"the `pEvent.iterator()` method. [Observables](https://medium.com/@benlesh"
"/learning-observable-by-building-observable-d5da57405d87) can be useful "
"too."
msgstr ""

