#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:69
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:71
msgid "pEvent(emitter, event, [options])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:72
msgid "pEvent(emitter, event, filter)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:74
msgid ""
"Returns a `Promise` that is fulfilled when `emitter` emits an event "
"matching `event`, or rejects if `emitter` emits any of the events defined"
" in the `rejectionEvents` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:76
msgid ""
"**Note**: `event` is a string for a single event type, for example, "
"`'data'`. To listen on multiple events, pass an array of strings, such as"
" `['started', 'stopped']`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:79
msgid ""
"The returned promise has a `.cancel()` method, which when called, removes"
" the event listeners and causes the promise to never be settled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:81
msgid "emitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:83 ../../source/p-event_readme.md:99
#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:157 ../../source/p-event_readme.md:214
msgid "Type: `Object`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:85
msgid "Event emitter object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:87
msgid ""
"Should have either a `.on()`/`.addListener()`/`.addEventListener()` and "
"`.off()`/`.removeListener()`/`.removeEventListener()` method, like the "
"[Node.js `EventEmitter`](https://nodejs.org/api/events.html) and [DOM "
"events](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Events)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:89
msgid "event"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:91
msgid "Type: `string | string[]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:93
msgid "Name of the event or events to listen to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:95
msgid ""
"If the same event is defined both here and in `rejectionEvents`, this one"
" takes priority."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:97 ../../source/p-event_readme.md:155
#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:212
msgid "options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:101
msgid "rejectionEvents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:103
msgid "Type: `string[]`<br> Default: `['error']`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:106
msgid "Events that will reject the promise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:108
msgid "multiArgs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:110 ../../source/p-event_readme.md:168
msgid "Type: `boolean`<br> Default: `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p-event_readme.md:113
msgid ""
"By default, the promisified function will only return the first argument "
"from the event callback, which works fine for most APIs. This option can "
"be useful for APIs that return multiple arguments in the callback. "
"Turning this on will make it return an array of all arguments from the "
"callback, instead of just the first argument. This also applies to "
"rejections."
msgstr ""

